description:
## Description

When using `mcptools::mcp_server()` (or `btw::btw_mcp_server()`) as an MCP server in GitHub Copilot Chat (Agent mode) within Positron, most LLM models (except grok-code-fast-1) fail with a 400 error when attempting to use.

## Error Messages

**GPT-4.1:**
```  
Request Failed: 400 {"error":{"message":"Invalid schema for function 'mcp_r-btw_list_r_sessions': In context=(), object schema missing properties.","code":"invalid_function_parameters"}}  
```

**Claude Sonnet 4.6:**
```  
Request Failed: 400 Bad Request  
```

**Claude Haiku 4.5:**
```  
Request Failed: 400 {"error":{"message":"The requested model is not supported.","code":"model_not_supported","param":"model","type":"invalid_request_error"}}  
```

## Reproduction Steps

1. `mcptools` 0.2.0 and `btw` 1.1.0.
2. Configure MCP server in `.vscode/mcp.json`:
   ```json  
    {
      "servers": {
        "r-mcptools": {
          "type": "stdio",
          "command": "Rscript",
          "args": [
            "-e",
            "mcptools::mcp_server()"
          ]
        },
        "r-btw": {
        "type": "stdio",
        "command": "Rscript",
        "args": [
          "-e",
          "btw::btw_mcp_server()"
        ]
      }
      },
      "inputs": []
    }
   ```
3. In Copilot Chat (Agent mode), select **GPT-4.1** (or any OpenAI and Anthropic models) and send any prompt that triggers tool discovery, e.g., _"List all available MCP tools."_


## Workaround

Setting `session_tools = FALSE` avoids registering the problematic tools entirely:

```json  
{  
  "servers": {  
    "r-btw": {  
      "command": "Rscript",  
      "args": [  
        "-e",  
        "mcptools::mcp_server(tools = btw::btw_tools(), session_tools = FALSE)"  
      ]  
    }  
  }  
}  
```

`mcptools` seems to have problems when connecting to MCP servers that run on FastMCP, for example the following `config.json` to run https://github.com/openags/paper-search-mcp:

```
{
    "mcpServers": {
      "paper_search_server": {
        "command": "uv",
        "args": [
          "run",
          "--directory",
          "/home/my_user/Projects/paper-search-mcp",
          "-m",
          "paper_search_mcp.server"
        ],
        "env": {
          "SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY": ""
        }
      }
    }
}
```

Yields no tools:

```
> mcp_tools("config.json")
list()
```

Using the same config on `.cursor/mcp.json` works fine and the MCP server tools can be used through Cursor chat, so I assume there is something not working on `mcptools`.
